course: dictionary
lesson: 8040
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. A dictionary lists each meaning, so you must pick the one that fits the sentence. Regime has two main meanings: a government, and a plan or set of rules you follow.
explain: When the words around it are about rulers, power or taking control, regime means a government. «Regime change» means forcing a foreign government out of power. The clues are overthrowing and foreign.
explain: When the words are about exercise, food or looking after your skin, regime means a routine, a plan you follow regularly. A training regime is a set of workouts. Ask yourself: is this about people in charge, or about a plan I follow?
fact: Regime means a government, especially one that rules strictly and does not let people choose.
fact: Regime also means a plan or set of rules you follow, such as a fitness regime.
fact: «Regime change» means overthrowing, or forcing out, a foreign government.
fact: Useful phrases: a strict regime, a military regime, a training regime.
fact: In May 1944 «Stalin's regime deported the whole Crimean Tatar people to Central Asia», and many died on the way and in the first years.
exercise: Coach says, «Follow your training regime every morning.» What does regime mean here? | A government that rules a country | A school timetable | *A plan or set of rules you follow | A type of weather
exercise: «In May 1944 Stalin's regime deported the whole Crimean Tatar people.» What kind of thing is Stalin's regime? | A holiday company | A kind of sports club | A plan for healthy eating | *A harsh government that did not let people choose
exercise: «Regime change» means overthrowing a foreign government. Which word in this phrase tells you the meaning is about a government? | *Both regime and overthrowing | overthrowing | regime | change
test: «Her skincare regime takes ten minutes every night.» What does regime mean? | A broken promise | A kind of cream | A government that rules strictly | *A plan of care you follow regularly
test: «The people wanted freedom, but the regime ruled strictly and would not let them choose.» What is the regime in this sentence? | *A government | A fitness plan | A school rule about lunch | A bedtime routine
exam: Which sentence uses regime to mean a government? | I stuck to my bedtime regime | The coach set a new training regime | *The rebels wanted to overthrow the regime | My gran follows a strict diet regime
